    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0535" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg455"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1369.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 1358, of the 26th
                    ultimo, relative to the expulsion of the Messrs. Eisemann, I inclose copy of a
                    letter from Senator Lodge, asking that the objectionable phrase “for police
                    reasons” be stricken out of the order expelling them from Germany.</p>
                <p>If that phrase could be eliminated so that it would not appear as if the Messrs.
                    Eisemann were criminals and were on that account expelled from the country, it
                    would be much appreciated.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d438-a1.xml" xpointer="d438-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
